== pitboard
Switch Claude Code, Codex and Claude Desktop between your own accounts without signing out, and see what each Claude Code and Codex account has left

Usage: pitboard [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status       What is signed in, and how much each Claude Code and Codex account has left (the default)
  enroll       Add an account: the one signed in now, or with --sign-in, another one
  use          Switch a tool to an enrolled account
  forget       Drop an account and its parked login
  stow         Put away the login Claude Code left in a file behind the keychain, then delete the file
  abandon      Give up on an interrupted switch that cannot be finished, keeping every login
  repair       Ask the credential store what parked logins are here, and account for every one
  adopt        Take over a Pitboard directory another computer wrote, keeping the accounts
  renew        Renew every parked login that is due, and nothing else
  schedule     Keep parked logins alive without running anything yourself
  log          What Pitboard has changed, and when
  uninstall    Delete every parked login this Pitboard wrote, the daily renewal schedule, the watch service and Pitboard's own files
  rename       Change the label an account is enrolled under
  doctor       Check that what Pitboard relies on still holds on this machine
  statusline   One line for Claude Code's status bar; reads its session JSON on stdin
  warm         Start the five-hour period of the accounts you choose as soon as the last one resets, while the app or `pitboard watch` runs
  watch        Switch Claude Code to another of your accounts before the one in use runs out, and warm up the accounts `pitboard warm on` turned on, for as long as this runs
  completions  Print a shell completion script
  help         Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

  -h, --help
          Print help

  -V, --version
          Print version

== pitboard status
What is signed in, and how much each Claude Code and Codex account has left (the default)

Usage: pitboard status [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

      --offline
          Answer from what was last measured, without asking anyone

      --fresh
          Ask about every account, even one asked about moments ago

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard enroll
Add an account: the one signed in now, or with --sign-in, another one

Usage: pitboard enroll [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          A short name for this account, such as `personal` or `work`. `codex/work` names a Codex account, `desktop/work` a Claude Desktop one; a bare name means Claude Code

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

      --sign-in
          For Claude Code and Codex, sign in through the tool's own sign-in, without signing out of the account in use: for the account in use, this puts its new login in use, and for another enrolled label, it renews its parked login. For Claude Desktop, Pitboard parks the account in use, leaving Claude signed out, waits while you sign in inside Claude and quit it, then puts that login in use under the label

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard use
Switch a tool to an enrolled account

Usage: pitboard use [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under, such as `work`, `codex/work` or `desktop/work`

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

  -y, --yes
          Where the service refuses the login in use for good, put this account's login in its place without asking; needed without a terminal or with `--json`

  -h, --help
          Print help

