== pitboard warm
Start the five-hour period of the accounts you choose as soon as the last one resets, while the app or `pitboard watch` runs

Usage: pitboard warm [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  now    Start an account's five-hour period now, whatever the span, through one short request Claude Code makes with that account's login
  on     Warm up an account from now on, within the span `range` sets
  off    Stop warming up an account
  range  Warm up accounts only between these times of each day, in this computer's time zone
  help   Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm now
Start an account's five-hour period now, whatever the span, through one short request Claude Code makes with that account's login

Usage: pitboard warm now [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

Arguments:
  <LABEL>
          The label the account was enrolled under, such as `work`

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard warm on
Warm up an account from now on, within the span `range` sets

Usage: pitboard warm on [OPTIONS] <LABEL>

