== pitboard warm range
Warm up accounts only between these times of each day, in this computer's time zone

Usage: pitboard warm range [OPTIONS] <FROM> <TO>

Arguments:
  <FROM>
          When to start, such as 06:00

  <TO>
          When to stop, such as 22:00; 00:00 and 24:00 are midnight, and a time before FROM runs past it

Options:
      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

  -h, --help
          Print help

== pitboard watch
Switch Claude Code to another of your accounts before the one in use runs out, and warm up the accounts `pitboard warm on` turned on, for as long as this runs

Usage: pitboard watch [OPTIONS]
       pitboard watch <COMMAND>

Commands:
  install    Have this computer's own service manager run `pitboard watch` from now on and at each sign-in
  status     Say whether it is installed
  uninstall  Stop it and take it away
  help       Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --at <PERCENT>
          Switch once a limit of the account in use reaches this share, from 50 to 99
          
          [default: 95]

      --json
          Machine-readable output: the same versioned JSON envelope for every command, whether it succeeds or fails

      --once
          Decide once whether to switch, from the usage Pitboard last measured, asking no service for usage, and stop. Warms nothing up

  -h, --help
          Print help

Anthropic's terms may cover automatic switching and warm-ups: https://docs.usepitboard.com/concepts/limits#is-this-allowed

